From db200521906d929aada9f9c6151507eba5e1bdea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mattias Walström <lazzer@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:43:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] zebra: keep queued kernel route deletes when a connected
 route comes up
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Organization: Wires

connected_up() drops queued kernel routes for its prefix so that a
late RTM_NEWROUTE cannot shadow the connected route.  The cleanup also
dropped a queued delete.  When an address is removed and a link update
for the interface is handled before the RTM_DELADDR, the address is
announced once more, the pending RTM_DELROUTE is thrown away and the
kernel route stays in the RIB after the kernel has removed it.  It then
wins over any protocol route for the same prefix, which is never
installed or redistributed.

Signed-off-by: Mattias Walström <lazzer@gmail.com>
---
 zebra/zebra_rib.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/zebra/zebra_rib.c b/zebra/zebra_rib.c
index bc8c94b9c7..d6849d8e53 100644
--- a/zebra/zebra_rib.c
+++ b/zebra/zebra_rib.c
@@ -4458,7 +4458,7 @@ void rib_meta_queue_early_route_cleanup(const struct prefix *p, int route_type)
 	/* Iterate through the early route subqueue */
 	for (ALL_LIST_ELEMENTS(zrouter.mq->subq[META_QUEUE_EARLY_ROUTE], node, nnode, ere)) {
 		/* Check if this entry matches the prefix and route type */
-		if (prefix_same(&ere->p, p) && ere->re->type == route_type) {
+		if (!ere->deletion && prefix_same(&ere->p, p) && ere->re->type == route_type) {
 			/* Remove from the list */
 			list_delete_node(zrouter.mq->subq[META_QUEUE_EARLY_ROUTE], node);
 
